{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history","id":963787,"title":"Great Scions of History","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T10:46:51-07:00","id":963787,"title":"Great Scions of History","content":"So, we now know that Julius Ceasar was a Scion. Does anyone else have any ideas for historical figures that may have been Scions?<br /> <br /> My idea is that William Van Alen, the architect of the Chrysler building is a Scion of Ptah. Maybe he's even buried there in the deepest, darkest basement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:34:43-07:00","id":963916,"title":"","content":"Julie D'Aubigny, Daughter of Aphrodite, who disappears from history because her torrid affairs with mortals and divinities alike got her caught in a tempest of divine vendettas which she at very least road out with style.<br /> <br /> Harriet Tubman, Chosen of Eshu Elegba in his Christian synchronized aspect.<br /> <br /> Bass Reeves (the real Lone Ranger), Son of Horus (as well as his mortal father)<br /> <br /> Otto Skorzeny, Son of Loki, who applied his trickster instincts to military tactics (even while his father was playing anti-authoritarian pranks on the Nazis)<br /> <br /> Jonathan Swift, Scion of Ogma (few generations removed, but Ogma revisited the line with him)... the art of the satire being reawoken in defense of Ireland deserves the obvious nod<br /> <br /> Perhaps a bit obvious, but Papa Doc could actually be exactly who he modeled his image on in the world of Scion<br /> <br /> Going off the Orphic Mysteries, Dionysus is a likely candidate to die and Incarnate - perhaps Lord Byron (with his bonus tied to Greece) is a good fit.<br /> <br /> ... ok one more Theoi.... Nikolai Tesla - son of Zeus, adopted by Hephaestus. Unfortunately many of his greater inventions worked on divine physics and could not be replicated by the mortal wielded tools of the era.<br /> <br /> Miriam Prophetissima (history's oldest known nonfictional alchemist), Chosen of Djeheuty (though notably while she respected and learned from him, she never worshiped the Netjer, remaining a henotheistic Jew)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-05-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:00:19-07:00","id":963930,"title":"","content":"Bruce Lee, son of Heracles. Guy did insane work out regiments and kicked like a speeding car!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:10:42-07:00","id":963935,"title":"","content":"Not Xuanwu? I don't mean to be ethnically prescriptivist - no question the Theoi get around and aren't hung up on race or nationality! I'd just assume Xuanwu to be closer &quot;domain&quot; wise to what Bruce Lee is famous for.<br /> <br /> Oh! What if he's blood of Heracles, who being Heracles promptly forgot he existed, and Bruce sought out and was trained by Xuanwu, so he ended up being adopted by Xuanwu into the Shen accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-05-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:16:38-07:00","id":963958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=963935#post963935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Xuanwu? I don't mean to be ethnically prescriptivist - no question the Theoi get around and aren't hung up on race or nationality! I'd just assume Xuanwu to be closer &quot;domain&quot; wise to what Bruce Lee is famous for.<br /> <br /> Oh! What if he's blood of Heracles, who being Heracles promptly forgot he existed, and he sought out and was trained by Xuanwu, so he ended up being adopted by Xuanwu into the Shen accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That could work. The reason I thought to use Heracles was not only because I didn't want to stereotype him, but because Bruce Lee is kind of renowned as <b>the</b> <b>martial arts master</b> to which all others are compared to. Which sounds kind of like what the Theoi stand for by being paragons of perfection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:05:11-07:00","id":964172,"title":"","content":"Alexander the Great was almost definitely a Scion, though who he was the child of is up to debate - he was deemed the child of both Zeus and Ra while alive, so... maybe he was sired by one and adopted by the other?<br /> <br /> Erwin Rommel might've been the child of a trickster god, though whether it was Loki (he's German), Seth (he's the 'Desert Fox') or someone else who made him is similarly up for debate.<br /> <br /> Shakespeare could have been the son of Brigid, or perhaps Abhean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 09-06-2016, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:10:31-07:00","id":964360,"title":"","content":"I like Lord Byron and Ada Lovelace as Scions of Hephaestus (note the club foot).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:21:16-07:00","id":964522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964360#post964360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Lord Byron and Ada Lovelace as Scions of Hephaestus (note the club foot).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting - if so Byron presumably resented his direct paternity a bit (along with the physical result), and idealizes some of his uncles (Apollo and Dionysus in particular) instead. Ada would have been closer with her grandfather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:43:34-07:00","id":964542,"title":"","content":"Joseph Bologne, Chevalier de Saint-Georges, scion of \u00d2g\u00fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:02:34-07:00","id":964551,"title":"","content":"Julian the Apostate, Scion of Athena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:18:56-07:00","id":964563,"title":"","content":"<b>Adolph Hitler, Scion of Hel:</b> Guy was two faced (a great, charismatic leader and monstrously cruel fascist), he built horrific prisons that few managed to escape from, and wanted his country to be populated by blond haired, blue eyed, perfect human beings (i.e Baldur)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:56:34-07:00","id":964631,"title":"","content":"speaking of world leaders, George Washington scion of Athena under the avatar of Columbia, mostly under Athen as a goddess of strategy in battle, as it would take strategy like hers for a young and struggling nation to beat an older, organised, and powerful one.<br /> <br /> And while I'm on the U.S. Benjamin Franklin scion of Dionysus with a certain fondness for his crippled uncle Hephaestus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:29:19-07:00","id":964659,"title":"","content":"My heroes. King Arthur scion of Arawn. Lancelot and Galahad...not sure exactly who they would be scions of but these three totally ruled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:12:29-07:00","id":964690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964172#post964172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alexander the Great was almost definitely a Scion, though who he was the child of is up to debate - he was deemed the child of both Zeus and Ra while alive, so... maybe he was sired by one and adopted by the other?<br /> <br /> Erwin Rommel might've been the child of a trickster god, though whether it was Loki (he's German), Seth (he's the 'Desert Fox') or someone else who made him is similarly up for debate.<br /> <br /> Shakespeare could have been the son of Brigid, or perhaps Abhean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rommel as a Scion of Set/Sutek is brilliant.<br /> <br /> Who laid claim to Lawrence of Arabia, do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:21:19-07:00","id":964759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964563#post964563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Adolph Hitler, Scion of Hel:</b> Guy was two faced (a great, charismatic leader and monstrously cruel fascist), he built horrific prisons that few managed to escape from, and wanted his country to be populated by blond haired, blue eyed, perfect human beings (i.e Baldur)</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that Hitler was two-faced makes me uncomfortable. To me it feels like it reinforces the lie that the NSDAP deceived its way into power and that the Holocaust was a secret - as opposed to what actually happened: they openly preached their ideology and were lifted to power by their supporters (and allowed by the passive majority).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:26:21-07:00","id":964765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964759#post964759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that Hitler was two-faced makes me uncomfortable. To me it feels like it reinforces the lie that the NSDAP deceived its way into power and that the Holocaust was a secret - as opposed to what actually happened: they openly preached their ideology and were lifted to power by their supporters (and allowed by the passive majority).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I can't say if it was a lie or not, as that's the story I learned from the history channel who has been talking about Hitler for like 30 something years straight. If it was, then Germany can at least save face by saying they didn't comprehend what was going on...<br /> <br /> If they knew about it and supported it... that leads to some very uncomfortable questions!<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, the other parts I pointed out fit well with a Scion of Hel. Especially the Baldur reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:36:33-07:00","id":964772,"title":"","content":"The public didn't necessarily know specifics about camps, but Kristalnacht could not have been more public. Nazi ideology Mien Kampf, and propaganda were not subtle about the racial &quot;threats&quot; to the nation - there was no secret at all about racial politics of the party before it's rise and the regime.<br /> <br /> The heroic minority certainly were well aware what would happen to themselves and to the families they hid if they were caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:38:51-07:00","id":964775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964765#post964765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they knew about it and supported it... that leads to some very uncomfortable questions!</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophers, psychologists, sociologists, and theologians have been wrestling with those uncomfortable questions for 80 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T22:37:07-07:00","id":964794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964690#post964690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rommel as a Scion of Set/Sutek is brilliant.<br /> <br /> Who laid claim to Lawrence of Arabia, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... Athena for the wisdom+war thing, maybe? Thoth for the desert+wisdom association? Amm, the ancient arabian god of wisdom and protector of the nomadic tribes for... rather obvious reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:59:40-07:00","id":964859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964765#post964765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I can't say if it was a lie or not, as that's the story I learned from the history channel who has been talking about Hitler for like 30 something years straight. If it was, then Germany can at least save face by saying they didn't comprehend what was going on...<br /> <br /> If they knew about it and supported it... that leads to some very uncomfortable questions!<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, the other parts I pointed out fit well with a Scion of Hel. Especially the Baldur reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I, as a historian (though still working towards my BA and not focussed on that era) and a German person, may weigh in here without derailing the thread too much, these questions are very complicated. I'll try to explain, but I should probably give some kind of trigger warning because there will, as always when discussing the Nazi, be some nasty insights into just how horrible human beings can be below. Or, as a TL;DR: Yes, the German people were, at least on a basic level, aware of the Holocaust/Shoah. The Nazis weren't two-faced, but pretty open about their hatred, although the specifics developed over time and were, in part, at least officially government secrets. The German people today are neither trying to save face nor are we avoiding uncomfortable questions, we're trying to make amends for this stuff on a pretty much daily basis. And making Hitler a Scion is an idea I don't like, for reasons.<br /> <br /> Now, the NSDAP did indeed come to power in part by popular vote and in part by using some very obvious flaws in the then young Weimar democracy, then declared (more or less in accordance with Hitler's legal powers as chancellor and/or president) a dictatorship that also met with popular approval. Now, why would that be? The racial ideology, while prominent, wasn't even really at the forefront of things in the beginning; it was about economic policy, about ending the Treaty of Versailles, about regaining national honour in the face of the WWI defeat - it was about strong, assertive leadership. Anti-semitism was still rampant in all parts of the Western world, as was racist and racialist rhethoric, so the NSDAP didn't even stick out all that much for that in the beginning. Their violent lashing out against communists was a lot more prominent. So I wouldn't say that the Nazis were elected for their racist views, but whoever voted for them (still the majority of the people) knew of those views and tolerated them at the least. As mentioned by others, the basic recipe of the new world order as imagined by Hitler was readily available in the form of &quot;Mein Kampf&quot;, the possession of which became mandatory in the course of the dictatorship - though I'd cast some doubt on whether anyone was really sure what was really going on in that book. From the excerpts I've read and heard in school and in TV documentaries, this book was nothing but a long, disorganised rant by what was at that time after all nothing but a badly educated prison inmate.<br /> <br /> And although racist laws came quickly with the rise of the Nazi dictatorship, things weren't that simple either. The Nazis didn't start shipping people to Auschwitz on Day 1. The Kristallnacht, that big, obvious outburst of violence, only happened in late '38, Auschwitz opened in '40, the star of David was introduced only in '41. (Please note that I'm not trying to play down the atrocities by pointing this out, I'm just argueing that the descent into this madness was gradual, in order to examine the relative obviousness of it that is at question here). By then, the dictatorship was already more dependent on public apathy than on public support, and dissenters were punished harshly (for example, the members of the White Rose, a student organisation, all got executed for spreading anti-Nazi leaflets at what is now my uni; they deservedly got every nook and cranny here on campus named after them after the war). Of course, there had been discrimination before, Jews being pushed out of the workplace and such, but it got worse rather slowly. We also have to recognise that the extermination of the Jews and other unwanted people(s) wasn't always the plan; this horrible &quot;final solution&quot; was only decided on as the most <i>practical</i> at the Wannsee Conference in '42 - other options discussed were e.g. shipping them all to South America, but in the end it was decided, as sickening as this is, that genocide was the cheapest approach. And views on the implications of a pseudo-biological concept of race differed greatly even within the topmost ranks of the NSDAP - my favourite example is Ernst R\u00f6hm, who saw &quot;inferior&quot; races mostly as sex objects and servitors rather than as pests and vermin. These terms &quot;pests&quot; and &quot;vermin&quot;, by the way, I take specifically from a document that's among those forced upon schoolkids in Germany the most: These words are, as such, not from any law or party propaganda, but from a &quot;fan letter&quot; written to Hitler by a little schoolgirl. I'm quoting from memory, but she basically writes: &quot;We don't show mercy to other vermin, why should we show mercy to the Jews? They should be treated the same way.&quot; So, by now even my own stomach is turning from dealing with this shit, so let's finally come to the main question at hand: How much did the population know of the Holocaust/Shoah, and did they approve of it?<br /> <br /> That little girl seems to at least point to the conclusion that a significant part of the population shared the sentiment that certain people (and although the focus was on the Jews and should stay on the Jews in any appraisal of this era, we shouldn't forget how hard other groups like Sinti and Roma, Slavs, homosexuals, the disabled, and plain political prisoners were hit) should just <i>be gone</i>. We also shouldn't forget, however, not only the many heroes who fought against the Nazis but also the fact of how quickly Germany turned into a functioning democracy after the war. So, what is the truth? Fanatics like that girl (or rather, at her age, the parents and teachers who indoctrinated her) aside, we must assume that most of the population was apathetic and intimidated rather than actively participating. We can also see this from the fact that the extermination camps were treated as a government secret - it was expected that most people would, after all, find this as going too far. But then, <i>did</i> people even know? I would, from the information available to me, say that if they didn't, they chose not to. Government secret or not, there were more than enough pointers for freedom fighters and dissenters to figure out what they were fighting for, so the rest of the population <i>chose</i> to ignore. Inmates of concentration and sometimes even extermination camps (there's a difference between those two types of camp that many don't realise: concentration camps were for forced labour, extermination camps for the active genocide with gas chambers and all; the extermination camps were mostly built on conquered territory, like Auschwitz in Poland, for the obvious and previously mentioned reason of keeping them out of the public eye) were lended out to companies as labourers (that's how Schindler got his chance to shine, while a great many of other factory owners, including the oh-so-great Wernher von Braun, chose to ignore the fact that those <i>slaves</i> being delivered to them were mostly on the brink of starvation) and the death marches often led through towns, not to mention all the train workers and such involved in the transport of prisoners. The horrified reactions of the German people to being confronted with the Holocaust/Shoah show, to me at least, that most hadn't fully realised the scope and actual grusesomeness of things, but the point stands that enough information to figure it all out was readily available. Shit, people could even see the smoke from the crematories at the camps. Let no one tell you the Germans were just blissfully unaware. You can't hide millions of dead and many millions more of those that barely survived, tortured, persecuted, crushed. Trying to explain it away like that is an enormous disservice to both the dead and the living.<br /> <br /> Now, why am I telling you all of this, discrediting my own people by admitting their guilt, both by participation and by inaction? Why am I not, as Nyrufa put it, trying to save face? Because, for all of the horribleness we committed or let happened, the German people woke up in the decades following the war, and (thanks to the Denazification programmes of the Allies as well) resolved to face our guilt in order to make ammends and never let something like that happen again (I proclaim proudly as rightist parties grab for power once again, as they are doing in all of Europe, but that's a story for another day). We didn't tear the concentration camps down and eradicated them from memory, we turned them into museums and every pupil in this country will visit one of those during a schooltrip some time along the way (as well, if possible, as a historical synagogue or Jewish museum). We commit more time in history class to this topic than to any other. We have monuments at every corner, the &quot;Platz der Opfer des Nationalsozialismus&quot; (&quot;square of the victims of national socialism&quot;, a wonderfully inclusive term I'm very proud of) here in Munich, a sprawling labyrinth of a monument right outside the Reichstag building in Berlin, and so many others I could spend days describing them all. Every dissenter and freedom fighter who fought against the dictatorship, as well as many prominent victims of the Nazis, have streets and buildings named after them. It's all not perfect, and it surely can't actually make up for what the Holocaust/Shoah did to the world as a whole, but unlike many other countries (for while I would never argue that the Holocaust/Shoah was not the most horrible crime against humanity you can think of, there are more than enough other, &quot;lesser&quot; ones that are treated with silence) we face those uncomfortable questions, and commit ourselves fully to giving back where we have taken.<br /> <br /> <br /> To finally return to the actual topic of this thread (sorry, this got a lot longer than intended), I would note that I, personally, am quite uncomfortable with the idea of Hitler being treated as a Scion. I don't like any approach that connects Hitler with any kind of magic or un-human origin, because that always tastes of apologetics to me. Seeing Hitler as a demigod or a demon or a wizard or anything just leads to conclusions like &quot;It wasn't the German people's fault after all, there were higher powers at work&quot; or &quot;Humanity isn't capable of such brutality after all, Hitler was not human&quot;. And those are the kind of excuses that are not only exactly what we are fighting against here, but that also create the danger of history repeating itself. If we forget that Hitler was human, we stop expecting that anyone, <i>anyone</i> could turn into the same kind of monster under the right circumstances. I think there are more than enough populist &quot;assertive leaders&quot; with some extreme and inhumane positions on the side running around right now all over the world for you to believe me that. No, Hitler was no madman, no unique monster, no demon, and no Scion. He was a ruthless, brutal dictator who had his best friend murdered for fear of him becoming a rival. He was an incredibly benign, even fatherly boss to his personal employees. He was a power-hungry warlord who lay waste to half the world. He was a gentle man to Eva Braun, who freely married him and followed him into death on the same night. He was the architect of the most terrible genocide in human history, who tried to &quot;purify&quot; the world by murdering not only &quot;inferior&quot; races, but even those &quot;impurities&quot; he found in his own chosen people. He was a vegetarian and an animal lover, who abhorred the hunt and cared lovingly for his dog. He was all those things, and that marks him as human. And that's the scary thing about him. We can't rest assured that he was something special or different that will never return. He was just a human who made certain experiences, made certain choices, got certain opportunities, and was thus formed in a certain way. And he was not alone, but stood on the backs of many like-minded men and women, who in their turn were supported by a climate of racial division and hatred that, in those times, held the whole <i>world</i>, not just Germany, in its grip.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for supernatural elements in the Nazi leadership, I'd recommend Heinrich Himmler to you. Probably not a Scion either, but as we've heard that there'll be mortal magicians and such in 2E, that fits him pretty well. Himmler was so obsessed with Germanic paganism and magic and witchcraft Hitler was embarassed of it. He wanted to prove that the witches of the witch trials were the real deal, collected a whole castle full of historical documents looking for real spells. Himmler and his folks also promoted stuff like swastika Christmas decorations and wanted to reintroduce Germanic paganism as the &quot;natural&quot; religion of the German people. Nothing against Germanic neo-paganism in general, but I think we can agree on the fact that those guys were more than just a little bit nuts. Have fun with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:22:11-07:00","id":964943,"title":"","content":"Public education in America is bull crap... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I share your sentiments on the Nazi's being involved with black magic. It seems every time we bring Nazi's into a story of some kind, they have to be involved with necromancy, demon worship, or even H.P Lovecraft cults in order to make them seem more evil than they already were. The trailers on Grindhouse included advertisement for <i>&quot;Werewolf Women of the S.S&quot;</i> I shit you not!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, onto more light hearted topics.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Bear Grylls, Scion of Davy Crockett<br /> <br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> I probably need to keep up with more celebrities more often...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-18-2017, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:00:02-07:00","id":965346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964943#post964943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I share your sentiments on the Nazi's being involved with black magic. It seems every time we bring Nazi's into a story of some kind, they have to be involved with necromancy, demon worship, or even H.P Lovecraft cults in order to make them seem more evil than they already were. The trailers on Road House included advertisement for <i>&quot;Werewolf Women of the S.S&quot;</i> I shit you not!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, all the Grindhouse previews were intended to be parodies of different exploitation and horror film genres; there, they were doing a more literal parody of &quot;Ilsa, She-Wolf of the SS&quot; and its ilk.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand...<br /> <br /> Lon Chaney is a Scion of a trickster god of the Tuatha de Danaan (don't have my book with me, so can't find the best fit, but one who is also a patron of the arts would also work, or work especially well). His son was similarly claimed by the same deity, hence their skills at disguise and makeup.<br /> <br /> Akira Toriyama is Japanese, but he was claimed by Sun Wukong and tasked with redoing Journey to the West to make the Monkey King look even more heroic. I'd say Akira Toriyama has succeeded at that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:47:17-07:00","id":965459,"title":"","content":"Moses, the Son of Set himself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:12:18-07:00","id":965628,"title":"","content":"Moses , thet Son of Set- that's an interesting story I am sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/205-songtress","name":"Songtress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar205_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:49:55-07:00","id":965640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=965459#post965459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moses, the Son of Set himself!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could go the route that Freud did in <i>Moses and Monotheism</i> and make Moses a Scion of Aten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:58:04-07:00","id":966044,"title":"","content":"That may be, but it seems like modern media feels like it can't make the holocaust interesting unless they throw in an eldritch horror. They were racists, a militarized bunch of racists. It's not like they're the first ones to ever pull something like that, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was going to add <b>Steven Seagal</b> on this list, but I can't think of what deity best suits his patronage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ghandi</b> - Scion of Ganesha. Guy lead a rebellion without having to raise a fist in aggression, and he won!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:54:55-07:00","id":966450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=965640#post965640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You could go the route that Freud did in <i>Moses and Monotheism</i> and make Moses a Scion of Aten.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: <i>Mumbo Jumbo</i> by Ishmael Reed, one of the more important sources for this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:54:24-07:00","id":967606,"title":"","content":"I don't know who he would be a scion of, but I am positive Rasputin would be a scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:36:21-07:00","id":968121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=967606#post967606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know who he would be a scion of, but I am positive Rasputin would be a scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps he's a scion of Turisas \u2026<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cdkBs0VCSX0\" data-code=\"cdkBs0VCSX0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cdkBs0VCSX0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> \u2026 or maybe that's just his cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:48:15-07:00","id":969588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=967606#post967606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know who he would be a scion of, but I am positive Rasputin would be a scion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would depend on what version of Rasputin you are going with. There is so much conflicting historography and folklore that you could justify a lot of different options via different portrayals of the man.<br /> <br /> If you're leaning into the folklore, I say make him a son of (or sorcerer who bought the favor of, thus being &quot;chosen&quot;) Marzanna or Veles - and he is millennia old and once called Koschei the Deathless, long before he was brought to Tsar Nicholas II's court to treat his son's hemophillia under a new name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:21:26-07:00","id":970768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=969588#post969588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It would depend on what version of Rasputin you are going with. There is so much conflicting historography and folklore that you could justify a lot of different options via different portrayals of the man.<br /> <br /> If you're leaning into the folklore, I say make him a son of (or sorcerer who bought the favor of, thus being &quot;chosen&quot;) Marzanna or Veles - and he is millennia old and once called Koschei the Deathless, long before he was brought to Tsar Nicholas II's court to treat his son's hemophillia under a new name.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly works! Not many (somewhat) recent historical figures have the sort of legend that Rasputin does, to the point even telling his story straight incites the imagination. If ever there was a famous scion, it would have to be him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:55:35-07:00","id":971761,"title":"","content":"Francis Drake could have been a son of Manannan mac Lir, though if he was I imagine that the Tuatha would have been pretty pissed with him for his part in the Rathllin Island Massacre. Given that he was born in Devon, it's possible he's a child of Manawydan fab Llyr instead. Or maybe the more obscure sea god of Nodens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:38:51-07:00","id":971774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=971761#post971761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Francis Drake could have been a son of Manannan mac Lir, though if he was I imagine that the Tuatha would have been pretty pissed with him for his part in the Rathllin Island Massacre. Given that he was born in Devon, it's possible he's a child of Manawydan fab Llyr instead. Or maybe the more obscure sea god of Nodens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the Tuatha have a Love - Hate - Hate relationship with their mortals (the mortals kicked them off the surface of Ireland, had various issues with them after that), they'd probably not care save for the fact that a peace was given and broken. The Tuatha are good about slaughtering innocents while out raiding, and killing youths if it comes up. But, you say you're going to do something, and then break your word running about killing people who can't fight back? That would be lampooned and mocked beneath the Sidhe, mockery and the sort.<br /> <br /> He might be an example of a Scion who went off the rails. Or one who forsook their Pantheon connections for Mortal ones, not abiding by the Tuatha morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:41:35-07:00","id":972313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I share your sentiments on the Nazi's being involved with black magic. It seems every time we bring Nazi's into a story of some kind, they have to be involved with necromancy, demon worship, or even H.P Lovecraft cults in order to make them seem more evil than they already were. The trailers on <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Road House</span> included advertisement for <i>&quot;Werewolf Women of the S.S&quot;</i> I shit you not!</div> </div> </div> </div> My thoughts on this matter are this; while I agree that claiming the Nazis had any backing from otherworldly powers feels like an excuse, it <u>CAN</u> make for some pretty interesting stories, and there <u>IS</u> evidence that at least a few high ranking members of the party had an interest in the occult. That includes such elements as the Thule Society:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/963811-call-of-cthulhu-mythos-elements-in-a-hunter-game?p=968394#post968394\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/963811-call-of-cthulhu-mythos-elements-in-a-hunter-game?p=968394#post968394\"> Call of Cthulhu/Mythos Elements in a Hunter Game? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/963811-call-of-cthulhu-mythos-elements-in-a-hunter-game?p=968394#post968394\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/963811-call-of-cthulhu-mythos-elements-in-a-hunter-game?p=968394#post968394 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've never really played Hunter and am doing some research as we speak to host a game to some friends and want to put in a Call of Cthulhu/Mythos feel to it. The book advertises that H.P. Lovecraft is a great way to run these games and want to go with it. However, most of the characters have had something that brought them into the light after seeing something horrific or something that affected them in a way to see the world in a whole new view. Is it still possible to test the Integrity of a Hunter? Would they still be shocked by the H.P. Lovecraft Mythos? Since most Hunters have powers, how can </div> </div> </div><br /> My take is that any otherworldly power that answered the Nazi's call only made <u>themselves</u> more despicable. The Nazis were monstrous of their own choosing; their evil was their own, but IF something from beyond chose to respond to/ally with/exploit that evil, that just makes that thing even more disgusting. And of course, a Great Old One would likely find one group of filthy humans holding themselves as superior to another group of filthy humans... laughable, or as close to our understanding of the concept of humor as they have.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think you meant <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0462322/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Grindhouse.</span></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:50:44-07:00","id":972316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=972313#post972313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, I think you meant <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0462322/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Grindhouse.</span></a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did. Only realized the mistake afterward.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I did not want to be responsible for derailing this into a conversation about Nazi propaganda. But I did notice a correlation between Hitler and Hel that would make him a potential Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2016, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:58:48-07:00","id":972321,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: Hitler loathed Himmler's fascination with the occult, as he felt it discredited his cause and valuable resources that could go to the military were instead spent on expedition to try and find proof of sublime energy beings in Tibet. The average German didn't care for any of this and neither did the average Nazi, with only Himmler and his men in the Ahnenerbe bothering with the crazier fringe stuff, and even then less so as the war went on. The most you can really get out of all this for Scion is some German interest into Norse/Germanic runic magic unless you want to go full pulp and have your Scions fighting in the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:02:26-07:00","id":972325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=972316#post972316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, I did not want to be responsible for derailing this into a conversation about Nazi propaganda!</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did I. Let's move on...<br /> <br /> I've seen more than one poster on these forums who was unaware that the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Henry_(folklore)\" target=\"_blank\">Ballad of John Henry</a> was based on a real person; a Scion of Hercules, maybe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:55:09-07:00","id":972348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=972321#post972321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most you can really get out of all this for Scion is some German interest into Norse/Germanic runic magic unless you want to go full pulp and have your Scions fighting in the war.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the Scions did fight in the war, I'd have to say it would be restricted to Hero level, or take place as top secret operations. I imagine that even one Demigod on the front lines would have impacted the war's outcome immeasurably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:39:03-07:00","id":972734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=972325#post972325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither did I. Let's move on...<br /> <br /> I've seen more than one poster on these forums who was unaware that the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Henry_(folklore)\" target=\"_blank\">Ballad of John Henry</a> was based on a real person; a Scion of Hercules, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: The most likely candidate for the real John Henry was a spuriously imprisoned convict who was probably around five feet tall. He's another good candidate for scion of \u00d2g\u00fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:21:26-07:00","id":975710,"title":"","content":"<b>Dwayne Johnson, Scion of Serqet:</b> Who knew <i>The Scorpion King</i> would be such an appropriate title... or an artistic rendition of his apotheosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T17:04:04-07:00","id":975740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=975710#post975710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dwayne Johnson, Scion of Serqet:</b> Who knew <i>The Scorpion King</i> would be such an appropriate title... or an artistic rendition of his apotheosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dwayne is part Samoan. Scion of <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C6PbWhWGUrY\" target=\"_blank\">Maui</a> is far more likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:06:17-07:00","id":976398,"title":"","content":"Alexander the Great: born Greek royalty, revered as a God-King in Egypt, with an empire that spanned Persia and touched India. The question isn't if he was a Scion, it's which of the four Pantheons he interacted with that he actually belongs in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:31:47-07:00","id":976407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976398#post976398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alexander the Great: born Greek royalty, revered as a God-King in Egypt, with an empire that spanned Persia and touched India. The question isn't if he was a Scion, it's which of the four Pantheons he interacted with that he actually belongs in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I already brought him up on the first page... It was one of the first posts, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Aleister Crowley</b> probably had something going on, though whoever his Divine parent was (Horus, maybe?) probably isn't in any rush to lay claim to him. Or... maybe he has some Titanspawn ancestry in him somewhere, and 'Aiwass' was trying to start a new Titan cult..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:43:14-07:00","id":976574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976398#post976398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alexander the Great: born Greek royalty, revered as a God-King in Egypt, with an empire that spanned Persia and touched India. The question isn't if he was a Scion, it's which of the four Pantheons he interacted with that he actually belongs in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Theoi writeup implies he wasn't one of the Yazata or the Devas - they've been condescending to the Theoi ever since Alexander's expansion ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:50:08-07:00","id":976580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976407#post976407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I already brought him up on the first page... It was one of the first posts, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Aleister Crowley</b> probably had something going on, though whoever his Divine parent was (Horus, maybe?) probably isn't in any rush to lay claim to him. Or... maybe he has some Titanspawn ancestry in him somewhere, and 'Aiwass' was trying to start a new Titan cult..?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be fun to view Crowley as a Netjer Scion who never had a Visitation, who thus spends his life chasing magic and all things Egyptian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:12:29-07:00","id":976620,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, but Theodore Roosevelt was clearly a Scion of Odin (I was on the fence between Odin and Athena until I remembered that TR was blinded in one eye after a boxing match)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:12:54-07:00","id":976651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=963916#post963916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (even while his father was playing anti-authoritarian pranks on the Nazis)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thank you so much. Loki is actually the antithesis of everything the Nazi ideology was about, so the whole &quot;let's blame it all on the Sly One&quot; narrative a certain first edition Scion book had going needs to make way for stuff like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=964551#post964551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Julian the Apostate, Scion of Athena.</div> </div> </div> </div>This fits so damn well. A man of learning and wisdom who turns out to be a capable military leader when necessary? Sounds right up Athene's alley. And he did hold Her city in high regard. <br /> Pericles as another result of Zeus being... Zeus?<br /> <br /> Ookay. Just in case anybody ever thought Hannibal Barca's real life was not tragic enough... Consider this.<br /> What if he was a Scion who never got a Visitation... <br /> whose divine parent was... say, Quirinus.<br /> Who used him to make Rome more powerful through adversity.<br /> A perfect enemy - strong, intelligent, charismatic beyond belief, adaptable and fearless.<br /> \u200bWho, in the end, helped Rome become what he wanted to stop it from becoming.<br /> ... Ouch.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:06:19-07:00","id":976685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976651#post976651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, thank you so much. Loki is actually the antithesis of everything the Nazi ideology was about, so the whole &amp;quot;let's blame it all on the Sly One&amp;quot; narrative a certain first edition Scion book had going needs to make way for stuff like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> This fits so damn well. A man of learning and wisdom who turns out to be a capable military leader when necessary? Sounds right up Athene's alley. And he did hold Her city in high regard. <br /> Pericles as another result of Zeus being... Zeus?<br /> <br /> Ookay. Just in case anybody ever thought Hannibal Barca's real life was not tragic enough... Consider this.<br /> What if he was a Scion who never got a Visitation... <br /> whose divine parent was... say, Quirinus.<br /> Who used him to make Rome more powerful through adversity.<br /> A perfect enemy - strong, intelligent, charismatic beyond belief, adaptable and fearless.<br /> \u200bWho, in the end, helped Rome become what he wanted to stop it from becoming.<br /> ... Ouch.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hannibal isn't allowed to be a Phoenician Scion, with that conflict being a mirror the war between their Pantheon and the Theoi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:16:05-07:00","id":976692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976685#post976685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hannibal isn't allowed to be a Phoenician Scion, with that conflict being a mirror the war between their Pantheon and the Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is very straightforward and neat, especially considering the meaning of his name. <br /> I was just trying to think of something particularly dramatic and sadistic, and that idea popped up.<br /> ... Alternatively, a Heroic Mortal who was just. That. Badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:18:21-07:00","id":976694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976692#post976692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is very straightforward and neat, especially considering the meaning of his name. <br /> I was just trying to think of something particularly dramatic and sadistic, and that idea popped up.<br /> ... Alternatively, a Heroic Mortal who was just. That. Badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda like Alexander as being a likewise incredible mortal. The Gods may fight over him, but his accomplishments were his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:32:26-07:00","id":976703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976694#post976694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Gods may fight over him, but his accomplishments were his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I have never thought of a Scion's accomplishments as not being their own. A hero's more-than-human nature is a part of them. They may have great potential, but the challenges they face are equally great.<br /> but particularly awesome Heroic Mortals are still a treat :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T16:04:20-07:00","id":976778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976703#post976703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I have never thought of a Scion's accomplishments as not being their own. A hero's more-than-human nature is a part of them. They may have great potential, but the challenges they face are equally great.<br /> but particularly awesome Heroic Mortals are still a treat :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm usually happy to have legendary mortals be just that. But Alexander was specifically called a Scion - the Greeks said he was a child of Zeus while the Egyptians claimed him the son of Ra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:45:57-07:00","id":976837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976778#post976778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm usually happy to have legendary mortals be just that. But Alexander was specifically called a Scion - the Greeks said he was a child of Zeus while the Egyptians claimed him the son of Ra.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always have Zeus as his parent, but his Visitation occurs once the Egyptians name his pharaoh and he becomes a Netjer Scion... or possibly once he becomes Persian <i>shahansha.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:29:04-07:00","id":976912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976694#post976694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda like Alexander as being a likewise incredible mortal. The Gods may fight over him, but his accomplishments were his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing for Napoleon, and frankly, Hitler, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","user":"evilnerf","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T06:14:02-07:00","id":977146,"title":"","content":"Harald Hardrada, Scion of Odin. A far-wanderer, clever ruler, and successful warrior who fell in battle. A good example also of not necessarily being of the faith of your divine parent, as I think he, Harald, was a Christman.<br /> <br /> Here is an excellent summary of Harald's life.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Fr6svdKp5fs\" data-code=\"Fr6svdKp5fs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Fr6svdKp5fs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 09-28-2016, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:39:04-07:00","id":978982,"title":"","content":"I thought of any easy one:<br /> Akihito and the rest of the Emperors of Japan are Chosen scions of Amaterasu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:15:04-07:00","id":979135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evilnerf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=976912#post976912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same thing for Napoleon, and frankly, Hitler, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I liked about WW2 scion was that even Loki, father of the World Serpent and the Fenris wolf, thought Hitler was a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:19:55-07:00","id":979165,"title":"","content":"In my game, Thales, Pythagoras and Euclid are all Scions of Athena. They hang out together in a realm that contains several geometrical Touchstones (notably The Pyramid).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:14:30-07:00","id":979187,"title":"","content":"Heraclitus, Scion of Apollo Loxias.<br /> Friedrich Nietzsche, Scion of Dionysos. <br /> Their spirits hang out and discuss philosophy (passionately) in a Terra Incognita, to which they were banished by Hades, who couldn't handle the pair anymore. Each has a temper equal to a nuclear explosion or several, and some strong opinions to get angry about. <br /> Both are probably on their divine parents' &quot;to watch closely&quot; list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:53:00-07:00","id":979217,"title":"","content":"Who would you makeSalvador Dali a Scion of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","