div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=980014#post980014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Nicholas Cage</b> is a Scion of Apollo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Apollo's a hilariously bad actor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:13:33-07:00","id":980519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meribson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=980311#post980311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apollo's a hilariously bad actor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't know whether Nicholas Cage is bad or not! That is a mystery without an answer, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F1XCUo_Uu8M\" target=\"_blank\">and woe be upon the mortal who tries to answer it!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:27:45-07:00","id":986918,"title":"","content":"For the knowledgeable and wise, from whom is descended the paisley park warrior, he who is to awesome to be contained by a name but we can call him, PRINCE","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:10:53-08:00","id":1007393,"title":"","content":"Hey, what would work better for Heinrich Schliemann?<br /> * A Scion of Hermes, because luck, great business sense and personal charm?<br /> * A child of either Clio or Mnemosyne herself, because this is such an obvious fit, and what the hell, humanity, why is your collective memory such a fascinating thing?<br /> * A Scion of Loki, because hey, just imagine all those self-important learned men dismissing the Iliad as a complete fairytale, while the obsessed amateur who just decided to trust the legend basically sends the status quo flying and proves that the world is infinitely crazier than most people believe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T22:59:25-08:00","id":1007583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=986918#post986918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the knowledgeable and wise, from whom is descended the paisley park warrior, he who is to awesome to be contained by a name but we can call him, PRINCE</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess it would take a celestial touch to be able to pronounce that symbol!<br /> <br /> How cliche would it be for JFK to be a Tuatha Scion? (As in genuinely asking, not as a rhetorical question.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:06:10-08:00","id":1009102,"title":"","content":"I think it would be pretty ironic if Charlemagne was an unawakened Scion who ended up spreading Christianity all over Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:57:38-08:00","id":1009379,"title":"","content":"I find it rather interesting that people think that only Scions have contributed to human advancement and civilization... that everyone of any note or accomplishment throughout human history had to be a Scion... at least in this setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, Scions can be remarkably influential... and are likely to advance society in some way... but are they the only ones who can do so? Is being a Scion the only reason someone can be extraordinary in this setting? True... even an extraordinary human will pale when compared to a Scion... but does that really diminish the accomplishments of extraordinary individuals who aren't Scions?<br /> <br /> Has there been no great innovations or significant accomplishments that weren't done by a Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:33:33-08:00","id":1009538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009379#post1009379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it rather interesting that people think that only Scions have contributed to human advancement and civilization... that everyone of any note or accomplishment throughout human history had to be a Scion... at least in this setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, Scions can be remarkably influential... and are likely to advance society in some way... but are they the only ones who can do so? Is being a Scion the only reason someone can be extraordinary in this setting? True... even an extraordinary human will pale when compared to a Scion... but does that really diminish the accomplishments of extraordinary individuals who aren't Scions?<br /> <br /> Has there been no great innovations or significant accomplishments that weren't done by a Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in any Scion games I'd run the only historical Scions would be people who were deified or said to be a god's child, like Alexander the Great. With a couple of exceptions (for example, I like to say that at least some Saints were actually Scions who were convinced that their powers came from the God rather than the gods), everybody else is just a normal mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:48:59-08:00","id":1009571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009379#post1009379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it rather interesting that people think that only Scions have contributed to human advancement and civilization... that everyone of any note or accomplishment throughout human history had to be a Scion... at least in this setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone has suggested that's the case, people just have their own lists of figures they would make Scions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T20:47:04-08:00","id":1009624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009571#post1009571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone has suggested that's the case, people just have their own lists of figures they would make Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, but people seem to be suggesting that every one who is remembered for some great achievement in history achieved that greatness by being a Scion. While much of this is open to interpretation, it does make you wonder if the only reason humanity has advanced at all is due to Scions. If every great contributor to human advancement from Imhotep to Edison, was due to them being Scions... what has humanity actually done on it own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:13:25-08:00","id":1009671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009624#post1009624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo, but people seem to be suggesting that every one who is remembered for some great achievement in history achieved that greatness by being a Scion. While much of this is open to interpretation, it does make you wonder if the only reason humanity has advanced at all is due to Scions. If every great contributor to human advancement from Imhotep to Edison, was due to them being Scions... what has humanity actually done on it own?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anyone suggested that. It's just if you take every single suggestion together you get to that conclusion, but no one is suggesting that that entire list would all be Scions.<br /> <br /> I generally just stick to figures who have a lot of mythology around them like Julie D'Aubigny, Rasputin, or Nikolai Tesla. The more well recorded a given figure's life and achievements are, the less I think they make good candidates for Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:21:13-08:00","id":1016166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009624#post1009624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo, but people seem to be suggesting that every one who is remembered for some great achievement in history achieved that greatness by being a Scion. While much of this is open to interpretation, it does make you wonder if the only reason humanity has advanced at all is due to Scions. If every great contributor to human advancement from Imhotep to Edison, was due to them being Scions... what has humanity actually done on it own?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anyone is suggesting that ALL of these people are Scions. Even if they were though, the people in this list are a very small portion of the whole of human achievers. If, in the fiction of this universe, there are people with magnificent powers given to them at birth, it makes sense that more then a couple of them became our figures of greatness. Heck, it would be far stranger if they DID exist, and none of them ever became famous or accomplished anything of note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:54:04-08:00","id":1016182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/963787-great-scions-of-history?p=1009624#post1009624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo, but people seem to be suggesting that every one who is remembered for some great achievement in history achieved that greatness by being a Scion. While much of this is open to interpretation, it does make you wonder if the only reason humanity has advanced at all is due to Scions. If every great contributor to human advancement from Imhotep to Edison, was due to them being Scions... what has humanity actually done on it own?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, Imhotep is canonically a Scion of Ptah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}